1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,020
Welcome back.

2
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:05,850
In this section we are talking about system services in Android.

3
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:11,490
Almost all the apps in an Android device communicates with system services.

4
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:19,110
Here is the architecture and diagram of Android and we could clearly see that System Services is a bridge

5
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:24,240
between the apps or app framework and the hardware abstraction layer.

6
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:30,780
For example, when we take a photo using camera, we communicate through the system services to the

7
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,640
camera hardware drivers.

8
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:38,910
There are mainly two categories of system servers, the media server and the system.

9
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:47,490
So media server handlers, media player, camera, etc. system server handlers, search window manager,

10
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:48,330
etc...

